cy forced the aura's hand in order  to honor their deals with foreign  Nations and also to keep the peace the  auras went on the hunt for crime and  that meant it was only a matter of time  before magical beings around Britain  decided that they didn't like the idea  of the ministry and its auras suddenly  telling them what was right and wrong  and devised as Gore was caught in the  middle of it when he was elected to  power the goblins revolted and sensing  an opportunity to overthrow the wizard  elitist government the werewolves joined  in as well but feister's Gore wasn't a  pushover he was one of the earliest  auras in the entire magical law  enforcement department with specialized  knowledge on the psychology and  weaknesses of every magical being in  Britain Gore managed to lead the  ministry to Victory and started A  Century Of Peace in the British  Wizarding Community From the Ashes of  that fateful Rebellion the ministry's  influence over the British Wizarding  World strengthened its laws and its law  enforcement became the bogeyman for  every magic user in its domain which was  most definitely a good thing it's easy  to look back at the years before the  auras and fill a Pang of nostalgia as we  think about all the Twisted Tales of  dark Wizards and forests infested with  evil vampires the world before the  aura's department certainly seemed like  a more adventurous place but for the  average Wizarding wedge who just wanted  to raise their family in a safe  environment the joys between a world  with auras and one without was a  no-brainer to them the stronger the  auras and the department of magical law  enforcement became the better after  Minister Gore successfully quelled that  Rebellion until grindelwald's Global  Wizarding war in the early to mid 20th  century the aura's department stayed  relatively quiet they patrolled the  alleys and Villages of the British was a  World killed a few werewolves and  banished countless criminals to Azkaban  but it wa